      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "Update: If your vrchat goes to install and doesn't fully install and says install again. Go on the 2nd shared apps account and install it there. Then it should fix your problem.",
      "viewerReactions": null
    }
  ],
  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2022-03-10T19:01:41.866Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "Okay so there is like 2 bugs on oculus side with that. So if they are on a 2nd account with the oculus tell them to log into their main ownership account on the oculus because the 2nd account is on a shared apps so you can't fully un-install vrchat. So you basically switch the beta back to the live the same way they got into the beta, but when they are back on the live. They un-install vrchat from the main owner account. (If they only are on 1 account. They need to make a 2nd account and play on the vrchat beta 1 time on the 2nd account then switch over the main owner account to un-install vrchat and re-install. One of those should fix it. (If this doesn't fix it then you need to send a support ticket to oculus and have them help you manually on the account bug side for apps.)",
